  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1121 PM CST WED NOV 11 2026\n\nThe first, weaker cold front is slowly making its way through the\nregion, as a very deep trough continues to build over the\nMidwest. The second, more powerful cold front will work through\nthe region Thursday night, and into Friday morning. This is where\nthe swing in temperatures will first be noticed, as highs on\nFriday will generally range in the low to upper-50s. By Friday\nnight however, widespread radiational cooling is anticipated\nunder calm winds, resulting in widespread frost/freeze conditions\nacross the state. This will likely end the growing season in many\nof our northern zones, where lows are expected to fall into the\nupper-20s. Here is where temperatures should remain through the\nweekend, with widespread frost expected each morning.\nTemperatures should slightly rebound into the start of the new\nworkweek, but only a few degrees in most locations, with\nwidespread frost remaining in the forecast into the middle of\nnext week.\n\nWhile these cold conditions will be the main weather story for\nmost of the next seven days, low rain chances may return to the\nforecast Monday into Tuesday. Here, a weak shortwave will develop\nalong the coast and move east, resulting in cold rain in some of\nour southern zones. Confidence in this scenario is currently low,\nas the placement and trajectory of this shortwave remains in\nquestion.\n\n/44/",
